menu "CrowPanel 1.28in board"

comment "Display"

config CROWPANEL_LCD_BGR
    bool "Panel expects BGR element order"
    default y
    help
      Swaps red and blue. y is VERIFIED on hardware (TrailCurrent Capstan),
      against a deliberate red/green/blue test pattern rather than a screen
      of UI chrome, which will not show a red/blue swap.

      Do not derive this from the vendor's LovyanGFX `cfg.rgb_order`
      (false on this board). It does not map onto esp_lcd's element order
      the way the name suggests -- deriving it from there gave the wrong
      colours.

config CROWPANEL_LCD_MIRROR_X
    bool "Mirror the display horizontally"
    default y
    help
      y is VERIFIED on hardware: text reads backwards without it.

      This flips the DISPLAY only. The touch layer has its own options
      below, and on this board they are NOT the same value.

config CROWPANEL_LCD_MIRROR_Y
    bool "Mirror the display vertically"
    default n
    help
      With MIRROR_X this gives a 180-degree rotation, for a panel mounted
      upside down. Mirror the touch to match.

comment "Touch"

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_MIRROR_X
    bool "Mirror touch horizontally"
    default n
    help
      Independent of the display transform, and on this board deliberately
      different from it: the display needs MIRROR_X, the touch layer
      already reports in the corrected orientation. Tying the two together
      gives a perfect display with back-to-front touch.

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_MIRROR_Y
    bool "Mirror touch vertically"
    default n

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_SWAP_XY
    bool "Swap touch X and Y axes"
    default n

comment "Rotary ring"

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_STEPS_PER_DETENT
    int "Quadrature counts per detent"
    range 1 8
    default 4
    help
      Counts the 4x quadrature decoder produces per mechanical detent.
      VERIFIED on hardware: 4. The EC3501 datasheet's "1 pulse per 2
      detents" would give 2, and at 2 every felt click moves by two -- its
      own section 4-2 (30 pulses per revolution per phase) is the one the
      board agrees with. Enable CROWPANEL_ENCODER_DEBUG and turn one detent
      to measure a different unit.

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_INVERT
    bool "Invert rotation direction"
    default n
    help
      Clockwise must increase. VERIFIED on hardware: this board counts the
      right way round without inverting (unlike the MaTouch 2.1in).

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_DEBUG
    bool "Log raw encoder counts"
    default n

config CROWPANEL_LONG_PRESS_MS
    int "Ring long-press duration (ms)"
    range 300 3000
    default 700

comment "LED ring"

config CROWPANEL_LEDS_MAX_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Maximum LED ring brightness (percent)"
    range 1 100
    default 100
    help
      Ceiling applied to every LED write. 100 is full scale, the brightest
      the WS2812s go. Lower it if the ring is too bright in a dark room
      (TrailCurrent Capstan runs this board at 40 on a wall).

endmenu
